From: RNSBox <rnsbox@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: sophgo: drop the EVB cam0_200 clock override

The override asked for 96 MHz on clk_cam0_200 but the bypass kept the
clock on the crystal, so it never took effect. With the bypass cleared
(previous patch) the divider register already yields a clock fast enough
for the modem 2 Mbaud; leaving the override in place would reprogram the
divider and pick a worse rate.

--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-duomodule01-evb.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-duomodule01-evb.dts
@@ -304,9 +304,6 @@
  * this mux in a state Linux can rely on, so pin parent and rate here.
  */
 &clk {
-	assigned-clocks = <&clk CLK_CAM0_200>;
-	assigned-clock-parents = <&clk CLK_DISPPLL>;
-	assigned-clock-rates = <96000000>;
 };
 
